{"kind": "inform", "reply": "This is general information. In the Philippines, 13th-month pay is a yearly extra payment for rank-and-file private-sector employees who worked at least a month in the calendar year. By law it is at least one twelfth of the basic salary they earned that year. For someone who works the full year, that comes to about one month's basic pay.

For Jun: Kako has his 13th-month pay as ₱48,000.00, the same as his take-home pay of ₱48,000.00 a month. Employers usually pay it in December, so Jun's should come this December. To be sure of the exact day, check with his employer or payroll.

