{"kind": "simulate", "reply": "With ₱10,000.00 a month going in, the Emergency fund would reach its target of ₱210,000.00 in 5 months. At today's ₱5,050.00 a month it takes 10 months. This is only a what-if, and nothing was saved.

How I ran it: the fund starts at ₱160,100.00, and the Credit card keeps getting its planned ₱4,000.00 a month. Mara's new pay brings your surplus to ₱25,050.00 a month, so even with ₱10,000.00 going to the fund, ₱11,050.00 a month would still be left unallocated. Your savings rate would go from 4.4% to 8.6%.

