{"kind": "look_up", "reply": "On the current plan, the car loan is paid off on Oct 1, 2028. That's 22 months from now. By then you'd have paid ₱38,914.35 in interest on it.

Why it takes that long: the plan only pays the car loan its minimum of ₱12,400.00 a month. Each month, ₱10,000.00 extra goes to the credit card, ₱10,000.00 to the emergency fund and ₱5,050.00 to the house fund. The credit card comes first because its rate is 3% a month, against 9% a year on the car loan. That's the avalanche order you chose. The card is paid off on Jul 1, 2027.

